.TH SENHUB-AGENT 1 "" "SenHub Agent" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
senhub-agent \- infrastructure monitoring agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B senhub-agent
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The SenHub Agent collects metrics, logs and events from the host and from
the services it runs, and ships them to PRTG, Nagios, Prometheus, OTLP,
Zabbix or the SenHub cloud. The package installs it as the
.B senhub-agent
systemd service, running as the unprivileged
.B senhub
user.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the service and probe status (\fB\-\-json\fR for a JSON object).
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose the install, configuration, outputs, probes and host in one pass.
Exits 1 on a warning and 2 on a failure.
.TP
.B version
Show the agent version.
.TP
.B console
Open the web console (\fB\-\-print\fR to show the address only).
.TP
.B config check
Validate the configuration, including the fragments under
.I probes.d/
and
.IR strategies.d/ .
.TP
.B config show
Print the merged and resolved configuration (\fB\-\-raw\fR,
\fB\-\-resolved\fR, \fB\-\-redact\fR).
.TP
.B config set \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Change one setting (http.port, http.bind_address).
.TP
.B license show
Show the current license. \fBlicense key\fR prints this agent's key and
\fBlicense activate\fR installs a license token.
.TP
.B refresh-unit
Refresh the installed systemd unit to the version embedded in this binary.
.PP
Run
.B senhub-agent \-\-help
for the complete list. Start, stop and restart the service with
.BR systemctl (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/senhub-agent/agent.yaml
Main configuration. Probes and outputs are read from the fragments in
.I /etc/senhub-agent/probes.d/
and
.IR /etc/senhub-agent/strategies.d/ .
Kept across upgrades and removal.
.TP
.I /var/lib/senhub-agent/
State and data.
.TP
.I /var/log/senhub-agent/
Agent log files, rotated by the agent.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation: https://agent.senhub.io
